"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/b66563e0-5f07-4515-9234-8ef0fe830b9c-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/use-a-qc-"
"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/b66563e0-5f07-4515-9234-8ef0fe830b9c-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Execute {#execute}"
msgstr "Jalankan {#execute}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we're ready to execute! We'll load Sampler, then send the job to the "
"backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita siap untuk menjalankan! Kita akan memuat Sampler, lalu "
"mengirim pekerjaan ke Backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Or, if you're using a simulator, you can uncomment and run this cell "
"instead:\n"
msgstr ""
"Atau, jika kamu menggunakan simulator, kamu bisa membuka komentar dan "
"menjalankan sel ini sebagai gantinya:\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process {#post-process}"
msgstr "Proses pasca {#post-process}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/use-a-qc-"
"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/3edb4a9a-2f9a-4713-8b16-b1294ba0ebf6-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/use-a-qc-"
"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/3edb4a9a-2f9a-4713-8b16-b1294ba0ebf6-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that the majority of counts are in either `01` or `10`, meaning that "
"when one qubit was measured to be `0`, the other was `1`, and vice-versa. "
"This is consistent with the Bell state $\\vert \\Psi^- \\rangle$ we "
"prepared.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita melihat bahwa sebagian besar hitungan ada di `01` atau `10`, artinya "
"ketika satu qubit diukur menjadi `0`, yang lainnya adalah `1`, dan "
"sebaliknya. Ini konsisten dengan Bell state $\\vert \\Psi^- \\rangle$ yang "
"kita siapkan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Experiment 2: Use `Estimator` to measure the energy {#experiment-2-use-"
"estimator-to-measure-the-energy}"
msgstr ""
"Eksperimen 2: Gunakan `Estimator` untuk mengukur energi {#experiment-2-use-"
"estimator-to-measure-the-energy}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we've seen how to sample a quantum state, let's use Estimator to "
"compute the energy of our Bell state $\\vert \\Psi^- \\rangle = "
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\vert 01 \\rangle - \\vert 10 \\rangle)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah melihat cara mengambil sampel keadaan kuantum, sekarang mari gunakan"
" Estimator untuk menghitung energi dari Bell state $\\vert \\Psi^- \\rangle "
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\vert 01 \\rangle - \\vert 10 \\rangle)$ kita.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Map {#map-1}"
msgstr "Petakan {#map-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a reminder, the energy of the system is determined by the interaction "
"between the spins ($J$) and the external magnetic field ($h_x$) as captured "
"by the Hamiltonian:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai pengingat, energi sistem ditentukan oleh interaksi antara spin ($J$)"
" dan medan magnet eksternal ($h_x$) sebagaimana ditangkap oleh "
"Hamiltonian:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each term in the Hamiltonian tells us how a certain combination of spins contributes to the energy. In Qiskit, we can represent these terms as Pauli operators, which are just labels for simple actions on qubits:\n"
"- $Z_1 Z_0$ acts with a $Z$ on both qubits.\n"
"- $X_0$ acts with $X$ on qubit 0.\n"
"- $X_1$ acts with $X$ on qubit 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap suku dalam Hamiltonian memberi tahu kita bagaimana kombinasi spin tertentu berkontribusi pada energi. Di Qiskit, kita dapat merepresentasikan suku-suku ini sebagai operator Pauli, yang hanyalah label untuk tindakan sederhana pada qubit:\n"
"- $Z_1 Z_0$ bekerja dengan $Z$ pada kedua qubit.\n"
"- $X_0$ bekerja dengan $X$ pada qubit 0.\n"
"- $X_1$ bekerja dengan $X$ pada qubit 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A `SparsePauliOp` in Qiskit is a way to store a list of these Pauli "
"operators along with their numerical coefficients. These Pauli operators are"
" the observables that we want the quantum computer to measure &mdash; the "
"quantities that tell us about the system. Using `Estimator`, we can compute "
"the average value of each observable on our state and combine them according"
" to the coefficients in the Hamiltonian to get the total energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"`SparsePauliOp` di Qiskit adalah cara untuk menyimpan daftar operator Pauli "
"ini beserta koefisien numeriknya. Operator Pauli ini adalah observabel yang "
"ingin kita minta komputer kuantum untuk diukur &mdash; besaran yang memberi "
"tahu kita tentang sistem. Menggunakan `Estimator`, kita dapat menghitung "
"nilai rata-rata dari setiap observabel pada keadaan kita dan "
"menggabungkannya sesuai koefisien dalam Hamiltonian untuk mendapatkan total "
"energi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that we omitted the `qc.measure_all()` line in our code. This is "
"because with `Estimator`, we don't need to specify where to measure in the "
"circuit. We will just tell it which observables we want estimated, and "
"Qiskit takes care of the measurements behind the scenes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa kita menghilangkan baris `qc.measure_all()` dalam kode "
"kita. Ini karena dengan `Estimator`, kita tidak perlu menentukan di mana "
"harus mengukur dalam Circuit. Kita hanya akan memberi tahu observabel mana "
"yang ingin kita estimasi, dan Qiskit mengurus pengukuran di balik layar.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize {#optimize-1}"
msgstr "Optimalkan {#optimize-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The optimization step proceeds as before, with the addition of making sure "
"our observables are also written in a way that the quantum computer can "
"understand.\n"
msgstr ""
"Langkah optimasi berlanjut seperti sebelumnya, dengan tambahan memastikan "
"observabel kita juga ditulis dengan cara yang bisa dipahami komputer "
"kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/use-a-qc-"
"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/09d2920c-65c8-4a3c-bdca-0da78f0ad0c1-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/use-a-qc-"
"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/09d2920c-65c8-4a3c-bdca-0da78f0ad0c1-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Execute {#execute-1}"
msgstr "Jalankan {#execute-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the Execute step, we'll load `Estimator`, then send the circuit plus the "
"list of observables that we want it to estimate to the quantum computer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam langkah Jalankan, kita akan memuat `Estimator`, lalu mengirim Circuit "
"beserta daftar observabel yang ingin kita estimasi ke komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process {#post-process-1}"
msgstr "Proses pasca {#post-process-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, in the post-processing step, we simply print the energy calculated "
"behind the scenes by `Estimator`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terakhir, dalam langkah pasca-pemrosesan, kita cukup mencetak energi yang "
"dihitung di balik layar oleh `Estimator`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is the energy of our state!\n"
msgstr "Ini adalah energi dari keadaan kita!\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Conclusion {#conclusion}"
msgstr "Kesimpulan {#conclusion}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we learned how to prepare a simple two-qubit quantum state "
"representing two interacting spins. We saw how to use `Sampler` to observe "
"the distribution of measurement outcomes and how to use `Estimator` to "
"calculate the energy of the state according to the Hamiltonian. Along the "
"way, we saw how the Hamiltonian encodes the interactions between spins and "
"the effects of an external field, and how different states can have "
"different energies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran ini, kita belajar cara menyiapkan keadaan kuantum dua-qubit "
"sederhana yang merepresentasikan dua spin yang berinteraksi. Kita melihat "
"cara menggunakan `Sampler` untuk mengamati distribusi hasil pengukuran dan "
"cara menggunakan `Estimator` untuk menghitung energi keadaan menurut "
"Hamiltonian. Sepanjang jalan, kita melihat bagaimana Hamiltonian mengkodekan"
" interaksi antara spin dan efek medan eksternal, serta bagaimana keadaan "
"yang berbeda bisa memiliki energi yang berbeda.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Extension to many spins {#extension-to-many-spins}"
msgstr "Perluasan ke banyak spin {#extension-to-many-spins}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So far, we have only looked at two spins, which is simple enough to analyze "
"by hand. In real physical systems, such as in a magnet or other complex "
"material, there are often many interacting spins. When the number of spins "
"increases, the Hamiltonian becomes more complex and finding the lowest-"
"energy state becomes much harder. This is where quantum computers can help: "
"by preparing different states and estimating their energies, we can explore "
"low-energy configurations more efficiently than classical computers for "
"large systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sejauh ini, kita hanya melihat dua spin, yang cukup sederhana untuk "
"dianalisis secara manual. Dalam sistem fisik nyata, seperti magnet atau "
"material kompleks lainnya, sering ada banyak spin yang berinteraksi. Ketika "
"jumlah spin meningkat, Hamiltonian menjadi lebih kompleks dan menemukan "
"keadaan energi terendah menjadi jauh lebih sulit. Di sinilah komputer "
"kuantum bisa membantu: dengan menyiapkan berbagai keadaan dan mengestimasi "
"energinya, kita dapat menjelajahi konfigurasi energi rendah lebih efisien "
"dibanding komputer klasik untuk sistem yang besar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A natural extension of this experiment would be to increase the number of "
"qubits to represent more spins and adjust the way the spins are prepared to "
"try to find the lowest-energy state. This approach is the essence of "
"variational methods, which you can learn about in the [Variational Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/variational-algorithm-design) course.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perluasan alami dari eksperimen ini adalah meningkatkan jumlah qubit untuk "
"merepresentasikan lebih banyak spin dan menyesuaikan cara spin disiapkan "
"untuk mencoba menemukan keadaan energi terendah. Pendekatan ini adalah inti "
"dari metode variatif, yang bisa kamu pelajari dalam kursus [Variational "
"Quantum Algorithms](/learning/courses/variational-algorithm-design).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are also other quantum approaches to studying ground-state energies "
"that go beyond variational techniques. These methods are not covered here, "
"but are introduced in the [Quantum Diagonalization "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms) course if "
"you're interested in learning more.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada juga pendekatan kuantum lain untuk mempelajari energi keadaan dasar yang"
" melampaui teknik variatif. Metode-metode ini tidak dibahas di sini, tetapi "
"diperkenalkan dalam kursus [Quantum Diagonalization "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms) jika kamu "
"tertarik untuk mempelajarinya lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Learning objective {#learning-objective}"
msgstr "Tujuan pembelajaran {#learning-objective}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Go back to the beginning of Experiment 2 and retry it with a different "
"superposition state. Can you find a state with even lower energy than the "
"one we used?\n"
msgstr ""
"Kembali ke awal Eksperimen 2 dan coba lagi dengan keadaan superposisi yang "
"berbeda. Bisakah kamu menemukan keadaan dengan energi yang lebih rendah dari"
" yang kita gunakan?\n"
